     },
     {
      "text": "هَلْ … أَمْ …؟",
      "tr": "is it … or …?"
     }
    ],
    "phrases": [],
    "synonyms": [
     {
      "word": "أَ",
      "register": "formal",
      "nuance": "prefix question marker (أَتُحِبُّ …؟); required before a negation: أَلَيْسَ …؟"
     }
    ],
    "etymology": {
     "text": "Univerbation of هَـ (ha-, an old interrogative, now أَ) + لـ (l-, an affirmative particle) (Wiktionary).",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Word order never changes in an Arabic question — هَلْ is all you add."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "Before al- it takes a helping vowel: هَلِ الْبَصَلُ طَازَجٌ؟ (not هَلْ الْ…).",
     "Not before a negation: “don’t you like …?” = أَلَا تُحِبُّ …؟ (with أَ), not *هَلْ لَا …"
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "Spoken Arabic often drops هَلْ and uses intonation alone; in writing it is expected."
    ]
   },
   "alts": [
    "هَلِ"
   ],
