    "phrases": [],
    "synonyms": [
     {
      "word": "هَلْ",
      "register": "neutral",
      "nuance": "the usual yes/no question word, a separate word; not before a negation"
     }
    ],
    "etymology": {
     "text": "From former هَـ (ha-), from Proto-Semitic *ha; cognate with Hebrew הֲ־ (hă-) (Wiktionary).",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Biblical Hebrew asks with the same old particle: הֲ־ (ha-) — the cousin of Arabic أَ."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "It is written together with the next word: أَتُرِيدُ, not *أَ تُرِيدُ.",
     "Before a word with al- it merges (آلْ…); beginners ask with هَلْ there."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "هَلْ cannot stand before a negation, أَ can: أَلَا تُحِبُّ الشَّايَ؟ — answer بَلَى (yes, I do) or لَا (no)."
    ]
